@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Context
+
+RFC 7396 §2 defines `MergePatch(Target, Patch)` in pseudo-code. The repo already has `isObject`, `setMember` (safe for `__proto__`), `hasOwn` and `cloneJson` helpers in `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a faithful, non-mutating, prototype-safe implementation of the RFC algorithm.
+**Non-Goals:** diffing two documents; validation (the RFC defines no error cases).
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **RFC 7396, not 7386.** The request cites 7386, which RFC 7396 obsoletes with the same algorithm (7396 fixes the media-type registration). The project context names 7396; the standard wins.
+- **Recursion mirrors the pseudo-code.** Non-object patch returns `cloneJson(patch)`. Otherwise start from a non-object target as `{}`, copy the target's own members with `cloneJson`, then process patch keys: `null` deletes, else `merge(own target member or undefined, value)`. A missing target member is treated as non-object, so nulls inside new objects are dropped as the RFC specifies.
+- **Own members only, via `Object.keys`/`hasOwn`**, with `setMember` for writes, so `__proto__` and `constructor` are plain keys.
+- **Results are built fresh**, so inputs are never mutated or aliased.
+- **No error class.** Every JSON value is valid input.
+- Known RFC limitation: a patch cannot set a member to `null`; documented in README.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Deep recursion on hostile deeply nested input; same as the existing `cloneJson`, accepted.
