+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents instead of JSON Patch operation lists. The toolkit has no way to apply them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the target with the merge patch applied.
+- Governing standard: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (`MergePatch` pseudo-code). The request cites RFC 7386; RFC 7396 obsoletes it with the same algorithm, so RFC 7396 is named here.
+- Not breaking: purely additive, no existing export changes.
+- Out of scope: generating a merge patch from two documents, and merge-patch media-type or HTTP handling.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: apply an RFC 7396 merge patch to a JSON document without mutating inputs.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function.
+- New tests in `test/json-merge-patch.test.ts`; README gains a section. No new dependencies.
